      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel a profound sense of loss when the silence of a shared space suddenly hits you. Many people navigate this emptiness by creating meaningful new rituals, like naming a favorite spot on the sofa or holding a small celebration on his birthday. Your feelings are a valid response to the absence of your partner, and it is okay to grieve those empty moments alongside moving forward.",
